384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (McCormack is an effective attacking midfielder in possession. He provides direct goal threat, carries the ball well and has enough passing range to connect attacks. His 73% pass accuracy is not elite, but that must be viewed through the role he plays. Creative midfielders often attempt riskier passes in congested areas, and his 1.9 key passes per game shows he is regularly trying to create high-value moments.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
385 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (His dribbling numbers are particularly encouraging. Completing 1.9 successful dribbles per game at a 67% success rate shows he can beat opponents and progress attacks individually. He is not just a safe passer; he is willing to receive under pressure, shift away from contact and drive Bray into dangerous zones.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
386 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (The main technical concern is consistency of execution. His crossing accuracy sits at 29%, and while he offers useful long passing at 2.6 per game, the 46% accuracy shows there is room to sharpen longer distribution. Still, for a First Division attacking midfielder, his mix of goals, chance creation and ball carrying is very strong.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (Off the ball, McCormack shows good attacking instincts. His seven goals from midfield indicate strong timing when arriving into advanced areas. He does not profile as a penalty-box striker, but he has a good sense for finding pockets and taking shots from central areas.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (Defensively, his 5.6 ball recoveries per game is a positive indicator. He contributes to regains and is not a passenger out of possession. However, his defensive profile is more about positioning and recovering second balls than dominant tackling or duelling. His 47% duel success and 17% aerial success show that physical contests are not his biggest strength.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 159 0 R
/E (He can contribute in a pressing structure, especially as a higher midfielder closing lanes and reacting to loose balls, but he should ideally be protected by stronger defensive midfielders behind him.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
